MAUS Privacy Policy

MAUS has no telemetry and no user account. It does not collect personal data and sends nothing to its developers.

Data kept on your PC only: your settings, score history, test results, error logs and the log of changes made by MAUS (so they can be undone), in %ProgramData%\MAUS and %LocalAppData%\MAUS. You can delete these folders at any time.

Network: this program will not transfer any information to other networked systems unless specifically requested by the user or the person installing or operating it. Network access happens only in these cases. During an audit, and during the optional weekly audit if you enable it: Windows Update search (Microsoft) and software update list (winget). For actions you start: Windows repair (DISM can use Windows Update), software upgrades and the optional PawnIO driver through winget, connection test, web searches (search engine of your choice), and links that open in your browser (MAUS help site, GitHub, vendor sites, YouTube). Some of these links carry a hardware model in their address; nothing is sent unless you open the link.

